- The reference Python code removes virtual nodes with `list.remove`, which is O(n). A production ring would use a balanced tree or a sorted structure with faster deletes. (General knowledge.)
- The sources don't quantify the moved fraction. Roughly 1/N of keys move when one server joins an N-server ring. (General knowledge.)

